#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Claude Code's status line for the Botropolis-City tree.
set -euo pipefail

usage() {
    cat <<'USAGE'
statusline — Claude Code's status line for the Botropolis-City tree

Usage: tools/statusline [--help]      (reads Claude Code's session JSON on stdin)

Line 1, this session:
  ▶ item N · its name · claimed when   when the session is named "item N", or
                                       runs in the worktree item-N
  <repo> <branch> · what the tree needs   N changed, ↑N unpushed or to land,
                                       ↓N to pull or to rebase, ⚠ unsigned
                                       commits, ⚠ a checkout not on main
  ctx N% · 5h N%                       context used, and the 5-hour limit

Line 2, the roadmap and the city:
  roadmap N open: N ready · ▶ claimed items · N blocked · N Aria's
  ⚠ N: its session is gone             a claim whose session is not alive
  rN · vX.Y.Z +N                       botropolis's revision, and its release
  city N needs you · N working         from botropolis's own daemon
  ⚠ N sessions share this tree         two live sessions in one working tree

It reads only local state and fetches nothing. NO_COLOR turns off colour
and links. `make statusline` at the meta root wires it into each checked-out
repository's .claude/settings.local.json.
USAGE
}

[ "${1:-}" = "--help" ] && { usage; exit 0; }
exec python3 -B "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0")")/statusline.py"
